  "answer": "I'll start by looking at the workspace.\nThe bug is clear: `add` subtracts. Let me fix it.\nFixed and verified.\n\n**The defect:** `src/add.ts` implemented `add` with subtraction (`return a - b`), so every result was off by `2b`. Signed inputs made it easy to miss: it only happened to look right where `b` was `0`.\n\n**The fix:** changed the operator to `a + b` — a one-character change:\n\n```ts\nexport function add(a: number, b: number) { return a + b }\n```\n\n**Constraints respected:**\n- Public signature `add(a: number, b: number)` unchanged.\n- `test/oracle.test.ts`, `package.json`, and `AGENTS.md` untouched; no config added and no test runner replaced (used the existing `bun test`).\n\n**Test result:** `bun test` → 1 pass, 0 fail, 5 `expect()` calls across `test/oracle.test.ts`. The suite covers `[2,3,5]`, `[-2,3,1]`, `[0,0,0]`, `[-5,-7,-12]`, and `[99,1,100]`, all passing."
